A||||5||Eric||A Day of Autocrossing||||1||
Z||000000||Eric||06-10-2001||09:08 PM||||Today was the second points event for the Ohio Vally region SCCA autocross club.  About 100 cars showed up, and mine happened to be the ONLY Fiero in attendence.  There are usually a couple other Fieros there, but not this time.  Could I perform under the pressure?  As it became apparent, I couldn't.  I finished last in class for CSP.  The only thing I can make excuses about is the fact that I was the only one on street tires.  So, in reality, my performance wasn't too bad.  <P>I ran the course five times.  I gradually improved my times over the course of the day.  On my final run I seemed to put everything together (I even put on a show for the corner workers).  <P>That final lap I attacked the course using all the power my little six had.  I was feeling very good about my run until the second to last corner.  I went into this left-hander way too hot.  And when I lifted and braked, the back end really came around.  I must have been most of the way sideways, but I kept my right foot in it and rode that puppy out.  The mega, super power slide set me up perfectly for the last corner, fortunatly, and I finished with a high 41 second timeslip, my best of the day.  I had so much fun.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Hey, I spotted Taijiguy this morning going north on 71.  You can't hide from anybody with that big IMSA wing, Taiji  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||ChadMan||06-11-2001||03:20 PM||||Well, at least you tried!  It looks like the next event I could make will be the fun run on July 8.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Eric||06-11-2001||03:27 PM||||Chadman, the July 8 race will be the third points event.  They're doing the fun run on the 24 becuase it falls on the same weekend as the Mid-Ohio thing.<P>If you need any help with the steering rack, I'll be more than happy to lend a hand.  I know my way around the 88's front end pretty well now.||||reg||1
Z||000003||ChadMan||06-11-2001||04:15 PM||||Well, here's my dilemma.  I've got this nice little Coupe with fading paint, some loose front end components, a bad muffler and an engine that stumbles at idle.  It's otherwise fantastic.  I should probably do one of the following:<P>1)  Accept my car's shortcomings, give up any sporting pretentions and drive it as it is indefinitely, as it is a great daily driver and shows no signs of giving up the ghost anytime soon.  Total cost:  $0.<P>2)  Invest in new inner and outer tie rod ends to go with my Dickman rack bushing, then spring for an Ed Parks-installed 2.5 or a 3.4 conversion.  Total cost:  $2500-$5000.<P>I have been scratching my head over this for so damn long it's not even funny.  (Though 87ECO5, Boilermaker, WTIII and the rest of the IndyOhio guys think it's funny...)<P>Every time I get my mind mind up, I change it.  I am pathetic.  Thanks!||||reg||5
Z||000004||rogergarrison||06-11-2001||05:09 PM||||just too much going on for me. going to Mid Ohio for Vintage Gran Prix, July 8 is the Len Imke/ Byers Dublin car show..... btw only Tweety-bird/hubby showed up for the Road Rally, they had the winning hand for a while. We had a really poor turn out. Tks for coming Tweety, hope you had a good time. <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Eric||06-11-2001||05:16 PM||||A 3.4 would be very nice in an 88 coupe.  I too think it would be a little pricy to go that route though.  If I were you, I would just go ahead and make the car handle like it should.  You could get some GT or Formula springs and swaybars for cheap, rebush with poly, and put some good shocks on.  In the end you would have a wonderfully handling car that's fun to drive (if you don't pay too much attention to your right foot).||||reg||1
